---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import EmailRequest from "@/components/ui/EmailRequest.astro";
import { getNavLink } from "@/lib/blog-helpers";
import { site } from "@/data/focuslab";
---

<PageLayout
	meta={{
		title: "Jobs",
		description:
			"Working at Focus Lab, a small independent product studio in Islamabad. Open roles, how we work, and what we look for in a hire.",
	}}
>
	<div class="page">
		<div class="page__headline">
			<p class="page__kicker">Jobs</p>
			<h1>Working at Focus Lab</h1>
			<p>Openings, notifications, and what it is like to work here.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="jobs">
			<div class="jobs__container">
				<div class="jobs__job">
					<p><em>We don't have any open positions right now.</em></p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="signup signup--jobs content">
				<h2>Request job notifications by email</h2>
				<p>
					Hear about openings by email below, or <a
						href={getNavLink("/feed/jobs.xml")}>grab the RSS feed</a
					>. We never share your email.
				</p>
				<EmailRequest
					id="job-notifications"
					recipient={site.email}
					subject="Focus Lab jobs"
					request="I'd like to receive email notifications about Focus Lab job openings."
					hint="This prepares a draft in your email app. You must open and send it to request job notifications; this form does not subscribe you automatically."
				/>
			</div>

			<div class="jobs__content content content--jobs">
				<h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					A small studio that builds its own products and answers to the people who use them.
				</p>
				<p>
					Focus Lab is a product studio in Islamabad. We build and run Urban Events for ticketing, WorkProof for workforce analytics, and Fixer for production errors. Once in a while we partner with a team when the fit is right.
				</p>
				<p>
					We work with Shopify, Cloudflare, Framer, Astro, React, TypeScript, Node.js, PostgreSQL,
					Stripe, and OpenAI or Anthropic.
				</p>
				<p>We're independent and self-funded.</p>

				<h2 id="who-you-are">Who you are</h2>
				<p class="lede">Self-directed and plain-spoken. Let's talk.</p>
				<div class="pairs">
					<div>
						<h3>You own the whole thing.</h3>
						<p>You're a manager of one. You can take a rough goal, break it down, and ship without someone checking in on you every day.</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3>You write plainly.</h3>
						<p>You say what you mean, and you communicate early — especially when something isn't working.</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3>You go to the end of it.</h3>
						<p>You're comfortable owning a product from a first sketch to a running service. When something breaks, you look into it.</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h3>You care about craft and outcome.</h3>
						<p>Not just the ticket. You'd rather ship the right thing late than the wrong thing on time.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<p>
					We don't care where you studied or worked. We care about what you can do now, how you'll grow, and how you treat the people you work with.
				</p>

				<h2 id="how-we-work">How we work</h2>
				<p class="lede">A calm, low-distraction environment where you can do your best work.</p>
				<p>
					We work in small, independent teams and give people room to own their part. Fewer
					meetings, less email, fewer interruptions.
				</p>

				<table class="ledger">
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Day</th>
							<td>Eight hours. That's the whole expectation.</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Week</th>
							<td>Forty hours, and we protect them.</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Meetings</th>
							<td> A weekly one, kept short. Everything else is a document. </td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Location</th>
							<td>
								Remote-friendly, with a home base in Islamabad. We gather in person when it's worth
								it.
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Company</th>
							<td>
								Independent and self-funded. We make more than we spend, and we keep the team small
								on purpose.
							</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>

				<p>We answer to our users, not a board.</p>

			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
